  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Song of Solomon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 7,
    "summary": "The song of love continues.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "How beautiful are thy feet with shoes, O prince’s daughter! the joints of thy thighs are like jewels, the work of the hands of a cunning workman.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:1",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy navel is like a round goblet, which wanteth not liquor: thy belly is like an heap of wheat set about with lilies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:2",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy two breasts are like two young roes that are twins.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:3",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy neck is as a tower of ivory; thine eyes like the fishpools in Heshbon, by the gate of Bath-rabbim: thy nose is as the tower of Lebanon which looketh toward Damascus.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 11
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 114
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:4",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Thine head upon thee is like Carmel, and the hair of thine head like purple; the king is held in the galleries.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:5",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "How fair and how pleasant art thou, O love, for delights!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:6",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "This thy stature is like to a palm tree, and thy breasts to clusters of grapes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:7",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "I said, I will go up to the palm tree, I will take hold of the boughs thereof: now also thy breasts shall be as clusters of the vine, and the smell of thy nose like apples;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:8",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And the roof of thy mouth like the best wine for my beloved, that goeth down sweetly, causing the lips of those that are asleep to speak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:9",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "I am my beloved’s, and his desire is toward me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 4
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:10",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field; let us lodge in the villages.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:11",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us get up early to the vineyards; let us see if the vine flourish, whether the tender grape appear, and the pomegranates bud forth: there will I give thee my loves.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 78
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:12",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "The mandrakes give a smell, and at our gates are all manner of pleasant fruits, new and old, which I have laid up for thee, O my beloved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 98
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 7:13",
        "book": "Song of Solomon",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 13
      }
    ]
  },
